    "geometryProvenance": "editorial_reconstruction",
    "justification": "The KAN-351 ledger records the geometry position of every instrument here: no_geometry, commission_geometry_required, map_not_georeferenced or annex_map_unacquired. Not one of the eight has delimitation linework this project can use, and tracing a modern boundary in its place would launder a 1947 line into an 1829 claim. These corridors are therefore drawn, declared editorial, given low confidence, and attributed to the phase they belong to, so the Atlas can show what each settlement moved without implying anyone has measured it. Competing lines for one moment are kept as separate features and never averaged.",
